      "id": 120489,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-11-11T17:23:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"AlexxKay\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> AlexxKay:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In a recent rules discussion an acquaintance made the claim that any given card can only redirect a specific packet of damage once. Last I saw, (compiled in Spiff's FAQ), that was not the case: <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/rules-answers-from-chris-at-pax-4082\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/rules-answers-from-chris-at-pax-4082</a> . Did this change at some point when I wasn't paying attention (it was over a year ago)?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I used to think that way and had somehow convinced myself that the one redirect per card per dealing of damage was actually a rule, or at least a really useful heuristic, but it has since been ruled differently, as noted in Spiff's FAQ.</p>",
